--- NEW
.export OptGuillotine
.import Talk_norm, Talk_CoOGuy

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;;
;;  NPC Guillotine
;;
;;    Talking to an ordinary townsperson removes them from the map.  The
;;  behaviour already exists: Talk_CoOGuy is the Coneria sage, who hides
;;  himself and then prints his line, which is exactly what is wanted.  So
;;  this is a substitution rather than new code -- when the flag is on and
;;  TalkToObject was about to dispatch Talk_norm, send it to Talk_CoOGuy
;;  instead.
;;
;;    The two plates are exempt.  They are Talk_norm objects, and removing
;;  them would take the Rod and the Lute out of the game.  The Earth Cave's rod
;;  plate showed what getting that wrong looks like: Talk_CoOGuy hides the
;;  object and then prints the line, so the plate gave its "nothing happens"
;;  message and vanished anyway, taking the staircase under it with the Rod.
;;
;;    The id has to be re-read from mapobj_id rather than taken from temp RAM.
;;  TalkToObject does back the object id up -- but into tmp+6, which it then
;;  overwrites with the resolved handler pointer immediately before dispatching.
;;  tmp through tmp+3 hold the object's four bytes of talk data, not its id, so
;;  the first version of this compared a dialogue byte against $16 and $17 and
;;  the exemption never fired.  X still indexes the object here: TalkToObject
;;  uses only A and Y after its own LDA mapobj_id, X.
;;
;;    It replaces the dispatching JMP rather than being called before it, so
;;  the call sites stay three bytes: bank $0E's object data is pinned at $95D5
;;  and TalkToObject sits above it.
;;
;;    In: (tmp+6) = the handler TalkToObject resolved, X = the object index.
;;    Out: does not return -- it jumps to the handler, as the code it replaced
;;  did.
;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

OptGuillotine:
    LDA OPTFB_GUILLOTINE
    AND #OPTFM_GUILLOTINE
    BEQ @out

    LDA mapobj_id, X    ; the object's own id, straight from the map object
    CMP #OBJID_RODPLATE
    BEQ @out
    CMP #OBJID_LUTEPLATE
    BEQ @out

    LDA tmp+6           ; only substitute for Talk_norm; every other handler
    CMP #<Talk_norm     ;   is doing something the game needs
    BNE @out
    LDA tmp+7
    CMP #>Talk_norm
    BNE @out

    LDA #<Talk_CoOGuy
    STA tmp+6
    LDA #>Talk_CoOGuy
    STA tmp+7
  @out:
    JMP (tmp+6)


ClearBGPalette:
